<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ernest Augustus I, Duke of Saxe-Weimar-Eisenach</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1688">1688</a>–<a href="/years/1748">1748</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Ernest Augustus I of Saxe-Weimar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ernest Augustus I was Duke of Saxe-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/weimar">Weimar</a> from 1728. When the ducal line of Saxe-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eisenach">Eisenach</a> died out in 1741 he inherited its lands, creating the united Duchy of Saxe-Weimar-Eisenach. He was an absolutist ruler with a passion for building and the army, and his grandson Charles Augustus later made Weimar a centre of German literature.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ernest-augustus-i-duke-of-saxe-weimar-eisenach.jpg" alt="Ernest Augustus I, Duke of Saxe-Weimar-Eisenach" width="320" height="525" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unidentified painter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ernst_August_I.,_Herzog_von_Sachsen-Weimar-Eisenach.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
